  "notes": "ばかり is a particle with two main uses: indicating something just happened, or indicating excess/limitation.\n\nTWO MAIN MEANINGS:\n1. Just (did): Verb-た + ばかり\n2. Nothing but / only: Noun + ばかり\n\nPATTERN 1 - \"JUST DID\":\n- {来|き}たばかり: just arrived\n- {買|か}ったばかり: just bought\n- {始|はじ}まったばかり: just started\n\nPATTERN 2 - \"NOTHING BUT\":\n- {肉|にく}ばかり{食|た}べる: eat nothing but meat\n- {遊|あそ}んでばかりいる: do nothing but play\n- {文句|もんく}ばかり{言|い}う: do nothing but complain\n\nVARIANTS:\n- ばかり: standard\n- ばっかり/ばっか: casual spoken forms\n\nNOTE:\nThe \"nothing but\" usage often carries a negative or critical nuance.",
